				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1510,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Supply missing INativeWindowConfiguration fields in sandbox config\n\nAdd eight non-optional fields to the `ConstructSandboxConfiguration` JSON blob that VS Code's `NativeWorkbenchEnvironmentService` and related environment service layers access without null-checks:\n\n- `perfMarks`, `loggers` — empty arrays expected by performance-mark collection and logger initialization pathways.\n- `colorScheme` — default `{ dark: false, highContrast: false }` used early in startup before the real theme is resolved.\n- `mainPid` — the current process ID, consumed by process-tree and crash-reporter logic.\n- `os` — includes `release`, `hostname`, and `arch` derived from `std::env::consts`, required by platform-conditional feature gating in the workbench.\n- `dataFolderName` / `sharedDataFolderName` — set to `.fiddee` (or the `ProductDataFolderName` env var), preventing `URI.joinPath(userHome, undefined, \"extensions\")` from throwing a TypeError in `extensionsPath` and `appSharedDataHome`.\n- `version` — read from `ProductVersion` env var, defaulting to `1.0.0`, used by extension compatibility checks and telemetry reporting.\n\nMissing any of these causes crashes during extension host initialization and workbench service construction. Body uses trailing comma syntax consistently.",
			"SHA": "0066703567eaf9dd4ae8579009011dbc6b79318a"
		}
	],
